What this licence covers, and what it does not

The MIT licence above covers this repository's own files: the integration
under waterbox/, the tests, the documents and the build scripts.

It does NOT cover the engine or the game's logic:

  - The engine is the RSDKv5 decompilation
    (github.com/RSDKModding/RSDKv5-Decompilation, the submodule
    extern/RSDKv5), a decompilation of Evening Star's Retro Engine v5, under
    the "RSDKv5(U) DECOMPILATION SOURCE CODE LICENSE v2.1", whose text is in
    LICENSE-RSDK.txt and in every package. The files in patches/ change the
    decompilation's source, so they are modified copies of it and are under
    those terms too.
  - The game's logic is the Sonic Mania decompilation
    (github.com/RSDKModding/Sonic-Mania-Decompilation, the submodule
    extern/SonicMania), under the "SONIC MANIA DECOMPILATION SOURCE CODE
    LICENSE v1", whose text is in LICENSE-SonicMania.txt and in every
    package. It is compiled in unmodified.

In short, those terms allow copying, changing and distributing for public or
private use as long as:

  - any build of the engine given to anyone has the downloadable content
    off by default (this core is built with RSDK_AUTOBUILD, which forces it
    off);
  - nothing is used for profit;
  - the decompilations and the original are credited to their authors, and
    not claimed as one's own (original Retro Engine v5 authors: Evening
    Star; engine decompilation authors: Rubberduckycooly and chuliRMG);
  - no game asset is distributed (this package carries none: the game's
    data file is the user's);
  - the licence travels with every modified copy of the source.

A built package therefore combines this repository's code (MIT), the two
decompilations (their licences above) with the iniparser (MIT), miniz
(public domain) and stb_vorbis (MIT or public domain) the engine carries,
SDL 2 (zlib licence), libogg and libtheora (BSD-3-Clause); its effective
terms are the decompilations', and it may not be used commercially.
waterbox/package-licenses.json lists every part, and every package carries
their texts.
